<main id="top"><div class="wrap"><div class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Independent software architect & developer</div><h1>Complex systems.<br><em>Clear solutions.</em></h1><p class="lead">I architect and build enterprise-grade software that scales with your business. Two decades of turning ambitious technical challenges into reliable, maintainable products.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#contact">Discuss a project ↗</a><a class="btn outline" href="#work">Explore my work ↓</a></div><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>20+</strong><small>Years of experience</small></div><div class="stat"><strong>Enterprise</strong><small>Systems & products</small></div><div class="stat"><strong>End-to-end</strong><small>Architecture to delivery</small></div></div></div></div>
<section id="expertise"><div class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="eyebrow">What I do</div><h2>Engineering for<br>the long term.</h2></div><p>From early technical direction to complex modernization, I help teams make sound architectural decisions and ship software built to last.</p></div><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="num">01 / ARCHITECTURE</div><h3>Software & systems architecture</h3><p>Designing scalable, secure, resilient platforms with pragmatic technical foundations and clear trade-offs.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="num">02 / ENGINEERING</div><h3>Enterprise application development</h3><p>Building robust web applications, APIs, integrations and business-critical systems from concept to production.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="num">03 / TRANSFORMATION</div><h3>Legacy modernization</h3><p>Untangling complexity, improving performance and evolving existing systems without disrupting the business.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="num">04 / PLATFORMS</div><h3>Cloud & infrastructure</h3><p>Architecting cloud-native services, deployment workflows and operational foundations for sustainable growth.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="num">05 / LEADERSHIP</div><h3>Technical leadership</h3><p>Providing hands-on engineering direction, architecture reviews and mentorship for high-performing teams.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="num">06 / DELIVERY</div><h3>Product engineering</h3><p>Bridging business requirements and technical execution to deliver useful, maintainable software.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="work"><div class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="eyebrow">Selected work</div><h2>Built for real-world<br>complexity.</h2></div><p>Representative project types. Replace these examples with your own case studies, outcomes and approved client details.</p></div><div class="workgrid"><article class="project"><div class="projectvisual"><div class="diagram"><span>Client apps</span><b>→</b><span>API layer</span><b>→</b><span>Core services</span></div></div><div class="projectbody"><span class="tag">Architecture</span><span class="tag">Enterprise SaaS</span><h3>Multi-tenant enterprise platform</h3><p>Reference case study: platform boundaries, data isolation, integration patterns and scaling strategy.</p></div></article><article class="project"><div class="projectvisual alt"><div class="diagram"><span>Legacy systems</span><b>→</b><span>Migration</span><b>→</b><span>Modern stack</span></div></div><div class="projectbody"><span class="tag">Modernization</span><span class="tag">Cloud</span><h3>Business-critical system modernization</h3><p>Reference case study: incremental migration, risk management and improved maintainability.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
<section id="approach"><div class="wrap approach"><div><div class="eyebrow">How I work</div><h2>Thoughtful architecture. Practical execution.</h2><p>Good engineering is about more than choosing technologies. It's understanding the business, reducing unnecessary complexity and making decisions that hold up over time.</p></div><div class="steps"><div class="step"><b>01</b><div><strong>Understand the problem</strong><p>Clarify goals, constraints, stakeholders and the systems already in place.</p></div></div><div class="step"><b>02</b><div><strong>Design for the right trade-offs</strong><p>Choose architectures that balance scale, cost, security and maintainability.</p></div></div><div class="step"><b>03</b><div><strong>Build and validate</strong><p>Deliver iteratively, test assumptions early and keep quality visible.</p></div></div><div class="step"><b>04</b><div><strong>Enable long-term ownership</strong><p>Document key decisions and leave teams with systems they can confidently evolve.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="about"><div class="wrap"><div class="sectionhead"><div><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h2>20 years building<br>what matters.</h2></div><p>I'm Alex Morgan, an independent developer and software architect focused on complex enterprise products. I work with organizations that need both deep technical thinking and the ability to get things built.</p></div><div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:18px">Example capabilities — customize to your actual stack</div><div class="stack"><span class="chip">System design</span><span class="chip">Distributed systems</span><span class="chip">API architecture</span><span class="chip">Cloud platforms</span><span class="chip">Database design</span><span class="chip">Security by design</span><span class="chip">CI/CD</span><span class="chip">Technical strategy</span><span class="chip">Engineering leadership</span></div></div></section>
